```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    %% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    %% DIAGRAM 6 (NEW) — Confirmer Appointment Confirmation Lifecycle
    %% Shows: booking → tech calendar → D-1 queue → status updates
    %% Key rule: appointment stays in tech calendar throughout;
    %%           only its status field changes.
    %% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    participant Agent
    participant Supabase
    participant TechCalendar as Tech Calendar (technician_appointments)
    participant StatusLog as appointment_status_history
    participant DailyJob as D-1 Daily Trigger
    participant ConfirmerQueue as Confirmer Queue Page
    participant Confirmer
    participant Customer

    Agent->>Supabase: Book appointment (disposition = Booked)
    Supabase->>TechCalendar: INSERT row — status: pending
    Note over TechCalendar: Appointment is now visible<br/>in technician's calendar

    Note over DailyJob: Runs each night — finds appointments<br/>where date = tomorrow
    DailyJob->>ConfirmerQueue: Populate confirmation queue for today

    Confirmer->>ConfirmerQueue: Opens daily queue
    ConfirmerQueue-->>Confirmer: List of tomorrow's appointments

    Confirmer->>Customer: Confirmation call

    alt Customer confirms
        Customer-->>Confirmer: Yes, confirmed
        Confirmer->>Supabase: PATCH status → confirmed
        Supabase->>TechCalendar: UPDATE status = confirmed
        Supabase->>StatusLog: INSERT status change record
        Note over TechCalendar: ✓ Status updated in place — row not removed
    else No answer / couldn't reach
        Confirmer->>Supabase: PATCH status → no_answer
        Supabase->>TechCalendar: UPDATE status = no_answer
        Supabase->>StatusLog: INSERT status change record
        Note over TechCalendar: Technician still sees appointment;<br/>confirmer may retry later
    else Customer cancels
        Customer-->>Confirmer: Cancel appointment
        Confirmer->>Supabase: PATCH status → cancelled
        Supabase->>TechCalendar: UPDATE status = cancelled
        Supabase->>StatusLog: INSERT status change record
        Note over TechCalendar: Appointment remains visible as cancelled<br/>(preserves audit trail)
    else Customer reschedules
        Customer-->>Confirmer: Request new date/time
        Confirmer->>Supabase: PATCH original → rescheduled + INSERT new appointment
        Supabase->>TechCalendar: UPDATE original status = rescheduled
        Supabase->>TechCalendar: INSERT new row for new date — status: pending
        Supabase->>StatusLog: INSERT status change records for both
        Note over TechCalendar: New appointment enters same lifecycle;<br/>original marked rescheduled
    end
```
